{"rubric_version":"opencode-browser-856867996e73f7dcc5e39827bf2af7555bd63d40-judge-prompt.md","attempt":1,"prompt":[{"role":"system","content":"# WebVoyager Benchmark Evaluation\n\nYou are an evaluator for a web browsing agent benchmark. You will receive:\n\n1. **WebVoyager_data.json** — the task definitions (task_id, confirmed_task, website)\n2. **results.ndjson** — the agent's execution results (one JSON per line)\n\n## Your Job\n\nFor each result in results.ndjson, judge whether the agent successfully completed the task.\n\n## Evaluation Rules\n\n**PASS** if:\n- The agent's `final_answer` contains the specific information requested by the task\n- The information is factually plausible (e.g., a recipe with \"4.5 stars\" when task asks for \"at least 4.5 stars\")\n- Minor formatting differences, extra information, or verbose answers are acceptable\n- Partial completion counts as PASS only if the core requirement is met\n\n**FAIL** if:\n- `status` is \"error\" or \"timeout\" AND `final_answer` is empty or does not answer the task\n- The answer is wrong, irrelevant, or hallucinatory\n- The answer is generic (e.g., \"I found a recipe\" without providing the actual recipe details)\n- The agent failed to find the requested information and said so\n- Key requirements are missing (e.g., task asks for \"rating above 4.5\" but agent's answer shows a 3-star recipe)\n\n**NOTE**: If `status` is \"error\" but `final_answer` still contains a valid answer to the task, judge it as PASS.\n\n## Output Format\n\nReturn a JSON array, one object per task:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"task_id\": \"Allrecipes--0\",\n    \"pass\": true,\n    \"reason\": \"Agent found a vegetarian lasagna recipe with 4.6 stars and 150+ reviews, matching all criteria.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"task_id\": \"Allrecipes--1\",\n    \"pass\": false,\n    \"reason\": \"Agent returned a lasagna recipe but it does not use zucchini as required.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nRequirements for each entry:\n- `task_id`: must match exactly\n- `pass`: boolean\n- `reason`: one sentence explaining why pass or fail, referencing the specific task requirement\n\n## Important\n\n- Compare `final_answer` against `confirmed_task` from WebVoyager_data.json for each matching `task_id`\n- Do NOT skip any result — every entry in results.ndjson must have a judgment\n- Be strict on whether the core task requirement is met, but lenient on presentation\n- If the task asks for multiple things (e.g., \"find a recipe AND list ingredients\"), all parts must be present to PASS\n\nEvaluate all results now.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"WebVoyager_data.json\n[{\"task_id\":\"ESPN--10\",\"confirmed_task\":\"Check ESPN for the score and a brief recap of the latest college football championship game.\",\"website\":\"https://www.espn.com/\"}]\n\nresults.ndjson\n{\"task_id\":\"ESPN--10\",\"website\":\"https://www.espn.com/\",\"task\":\"Check ESPN for the score and a brief recap of the latest college football championship game.\",\"session_id\":\"eval-ESPN--10-9c8ad9532013\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"duration_ms\":523337,\"steps\":45,\"tokens\":{\"input\":187530,\"output\":13335,\"cache_read\":560111,\"cache_write\":0,\"reasoning\":10137},\"cost\":0.10586766,\"final_answer\":\"I have all the information I need. Let me provide the final answer.\\n\\n## Final Answer\\n\\n**The Latest College Football Championship Game: 2025 CFP National Championship**\\n\\n### Score\\n**#1 Indiana Hoosiers 27, #10 Miami Hurricanes 21**\\n\\n### Brief Recap\\n- **Date/Location:** January 20, 2026, at Hard Rock Stadium in Miami Gardens, FL (Attendance: 67,227)\\n- **Result:** Indiana completed a perfect 16-0 season and won the program's **first-ever national championship**, beating #10 Miami 27-21 in the CFP National Championship.\\n- **Headline:** *\\\"Indiana completes undefeated season and wins first national title, beating Miami 27-21 in CFP final\\\"* (by AP)\\n- **Key Play:** Heisman Trophy-winning quarterback **Fernando Mendoza** delivered the game-clinching moment on a fourth-down touchdown run — lowering his pads into a defender, spinning in a full circle, then launching himself horizontally to reach the ball over the goal line.\\n- **Score by Quarter:** Indiana 3-7-7-10 = 27; Miami 0-0-7-14 = 21\\n- **Notable Stats:**\\n  - Miami QB Carson Beck: 232 pass yards, 1 TD, 1 INT\\n  - Miami RB Mark Fletcher Jr.: 112 rush yards, 2 TDs\\n  - Miami WR Malachi Toney: 122 receiving yards, 1 TD\\n  - Total yards: Miami 342, Indiana 317\\n  - Turnovers: Miami 1, Indiana 0\\n- **Significance:** The victory ended Indiana's long-standing status as one of the historically losing programs in Division I FBS football — fulfilling Coach Curt Cignetti's transformation of the program in just his second season. The article notes the moment may be remembered as *\\\"Hoosiers\\\"* (referencing the famous film).\\n\\nThe path: Indiana beat #5 Oregon 56-22 (Peach Bowl semifinal) and #9 Alabama 38-3 (Rose Bowl semifinal) to reach the championship. Miami upset #2 Ohio State 24-14 (Cotton Bowl semifinal) and beat #6 Ole Miss 31-27 (Fiesta Bowl semifinal).\",\"tool_trace\":[{\"tool\":\"browser_start\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://www.espn.com/\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0dc9661a5715caed1abe7\",\"time_ms\":19455,\"output_preview\":\"# Browser Mode\\n\\nThe DSH browser plugin controls a real Chromium instance isolated to the current Agent Session.\\n\\n- DOM markers `[N]` are clickable and `<N>` are inputs.\\n- Match element labels or nearby text, and use DOM indentation to distinguish parents, children, and siblings; do not choose by mar\",\"status\":\"success\"},{\"tool\":\"browser_click\",\"input\":{\"elementIndex\":6809,\"expectText\":\"NCAAF\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0dc96b4f973f1bfab06a8\",\"time_ms\":6887,\"output_preview\":\"Clicked <a> NCAAF </a> Postcondition verified.\\n\\n\\n<!-- DOM_START dom1 tab:tab0 mode:full -->\\n(stateId: tab0-dom1)\\n## Current Page DOM Structure\\n\\n\\n<section></section>\\n\\t<div></div>\\n\\t\\t[208